 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Why did poet G\u00e9rard de Nerval walk a lobster through Paris?",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.267
  },
  {
   "text": "The lobster is named Thibault, and his leash is a blue silk ribbon.",
   "s": 3.567,
   "e": 6.935
  },
  {
   "text": "Ladies gasp, kids giggle, and a poodle barks at it from a bench.",
   "s": 7.135,
   "e": 10.192
  },
  {
   "text": "G\u00e9rard tips his hat and keeps on strolling, proud as a king.",
   "s": 10.392,
   "e": 13.402
  },
  {
   "text": "Then Thibault snaps at a pigeon, and the whole garden screams!",
   "s": 13.602,
   "e": 16.545
  },
  {
   "text": "A gentleman jumps backward, right into the fountain!",
   "s": 16.745,
   "e": 18.884
  },
  {
   "text": "So a policeman marches over and asks: \"Monsieur, why a lobster?\"",
   "s": 19.084,
   "e": 22.539
  },
  {
   "text": "But it gets worse. Thibault sits down, and refuses to move.",
   "s": 22.659,
   "e": 25.651
  },
  {
   "text": "A crowd circles them. Reporters scribble. Some people bet he's mad.",
   "s": 25.851,
   "e": 29.425
  },
  {
   "text": "Then G\u00e9rard finally answers.",
   "s": 29.825,
   "e": 31.314
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Why is a lobster sillier than a dog? It's calm, it's serious,",
   "s": 31.514,
   "e": 34.477
  },
  {
   "text": "and it knows the secrets of the sea. And it never barks.\"",
   "s": 34.597,
   "e": 37.227
  },
  {
   "text": "Right then, the poodle barks. Everybody turns and stares at the poodle.",
   "s": 37.347,
   "e": 40.872
  },
  {
   "text": "And that's why a poet walks a lobster through Paris.",
   "s": 41.072,
   "e": 43.533
  }
 ],
